#: ../../../users/proxying.rst:4
msgid "Using Proxies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/proxying.rst:8
msgid ""
"Syncthing can run behind a SOCKS5, HTTP, or HTTPS proxy. This enables use "
"behind some corporate firewalls, tunneling via SSH, and over Tor. The "
"Syncthing instance that is behind the proxy is limited to outbound "
"connections - it can not listen for incoming connections via the proxy. It "
"is however possible to receive incoming connections via :ref:`relaying`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/proxying.rst:16
msgid "Support for HTTP and HTTPS proxies via ``all_proxy``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/proxying.rst:18
msgid ""
"There is no graphical configuration to enable proxy usage in Syncthing. "
"Instead, an environment variable ``all_proxy`` must be set that points to "
"the proxy. The value of this variable is the proxy URL. For example, on a "
"Linux-like system::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/proxying.rst:23
msgid ""
"$ export all_proxy=socks5://10.20.30.40:5060\n"
"$ syncthing\n"
"[monitor] 11:25:39 INFO: Starting syncthing\n"
"...\n"
"[monitor] 11:25:40 INFO: Proxy settings detected"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/proxying.rst:29
msgid "Or for an HTTP/HTTPS proxy::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/proxying.rst:31
msgid ""
"$ export all_proxy=http://10.20.30.40:8080\n"
"$ # Or with authentication and encryption\n"
"$ export all_proxy=https://user:password@proxy.example.com:8443\n"
"$ syncthing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/proxying.rst:36
msgid ""
"HTTP proxies requiring basic authentication can be specified by embedding "
"credentials in the proxy URL. When credentials are used over a cleartext "
"HTTP proxy, a warning will be logged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/proxying.rst:40
msgid ""
"Note that this environment variable is *not* named with capital letters - it "
"must be exactly ``all_proxy``. The \"Proxy settings detected\" log message "
"indicates that Syncthing is using the proxy configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/proxying.rst:45
msgid "Disabling Fallback"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/proxying.rst:49
msgid ""
"By default, Syncthing will attempt a direct connection if a connection via "
"the proxy fails. This is desirable when moving frequently between a proxied "
"and non-proxied environment. However it may be undesirable if the intention "
"is to force all connections through a Tor proxy or similar. In that case, "
"setting the environment variable ``ALL_PROXY_NO_FALLBACK`` (with capital "
"letters) will prevent the fallback behavior. For example::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/proxying.rst:56
msgid ""
"$ export all_proxy=socks5://10.20.30.40:5060\n"
"$ export ALL_PROXY_NO_FALLBACK=1\n"
"$ syncthing\n"
"[monitor] 11:33:13 INFO: Starting syncthing\n"
"...\n"
"[monitor] 11:33:13 INFO: Proxy settings detected\n"
"[monitor] 11:33:13 INFO: Proxy fallback disabled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/proxying.rst:65
msgid "Caveats"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/proxying.rst:67
msgid ""
"Syncthing will use the ``http_proxy`` / ``https_proxy`` settings in "
"combination with ``all_proxy``. Proxies specified with ``http_`` variants "
"will be used behind the configured proxy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/proxying.rst:71
msgid ""
"If this is not desired, make sure to undefine the ``http_proxy`` / "
"``https_proxy`` variables for syncthing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/proxying.rst:74
msgid ""
"When using an HTTP proxy via ``all_proxy``, only outbound TCP connections "
"are supported. Non-TCP transports and listening sockets are not supported "
"through HTTP or HTTPS proxies."
msgstr ""
